{"lines": ["Ghost lights rise over a North Carolina mountain. And the government sent scientists to catch them. Twice.", "Brown Mountain, 1910s. Locals watch red lights float above the ridge nightly.", "In 1913, an official says they're train headlights.", "Nobody buys it. So in 1922, geologist George Mansfield camps there two weeks with a telescope.", "He tracks twenty-three lights. One flares, drifts, looks alive. Through the telescope, it never moves.", "The count? Nearly half were car headlights. A third, trains. The rest, fires and fixed lamps.", "Case closed? Not for locals. A 1916 flood stopped the trains for weeks, and a hotel owner said the lights kept coming.", "Decades later, university cameras watched the ridge for six thousand hours. Nothing unexplained.", "So are they ghost lights, or just headlights? Tell me below."], "words": [["Ghost", 0.0, 0.2], ["lights", 0.2, 0.52], ["rise", 0.52, 0.88], ["over", 0.88, 1.48], ["a", 1.48, 1.64], ["North", 1.64, 1.88], ["Carolina", 1.88, 2.2], ["mountain.", 2.2, 2.86], ["And", 3.38, 3.46], ["the", 3.46, 3.54], ["government", 3.54, 3.84], ["sent", 3.84, 4.26], ["scientists", 4.26, 4.6], ["to", 4.6, 5.26], ["catch", 5.26, 5.44], ["them.", 5.44, 5.76], ["Twice.", 6.26, 6.44], ["Brown", 7.44, 7.48], ["Mountain,", 7.48, 7.76], ["1910s.", 8.28, 9.8], ["Locals", 10.04, 10.26], ["watch", 10.26, 10.64], ["red", 10.64, 11.06], ["lights", 11.06, 11.34], ["float", 11.34, 11.68], ["above", 11.68, 12.0], ["the", 12.0, 12.2], ["ridge", 12.2, 12.38], ["nightly.", 12.38, 12.74], ["In", 13.38, 13.44], ["1913,", 13.44, 14.34], ["an", 14.52, 15.06], ["official", 15.06, 15.32], ["says", 15.32, 15.8], ["they're", 15.8, 16.04], ["train", 16.04, 16.34], ["headlights.", 16.34, 16.64], ["Nobody", 17.517, 17.8], ["buys", 17.8, 18.22], ["it.", 18.22, 18.56], ["So", 18.76, 18.98], ["in", 18.98, 19.16], ["1922,", 19.16, 20.06], ["geologist", 20.72, 21.28], ["George", 21.28, 21.72], ["Mansfield", 21.72, 22.48], ["camps", 22.48, 22.84], ["there",